{"name":"Fragrant Satchel","hex":"#a99fba","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fragrant","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Sweet-smelling; having a pleasant (usually strong) scent or fragrance.","Attractive."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fragrant"},{"term":"satchel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A bag or case with one or two shoulder straps, especially used to carry books etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/satchel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fragrance compound","blocks":[{"text":"A fragrance compound is a chemical compound with a pleasant odor. Fragrances affect only the sense of smell, whereas flavors can affect both the sense of taste and smell. Fragrances are often mixtures of individual fragrance compounds. Although many fragrances are derived from natural sources, many are synthetic. Fragrances are widely used in cosmetics and are the basis for a large industry."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fragrance_compound"},{"title":"Satchel","blocks":[{"text":"A satchel is a bag with a strap, traditionally used for carrying books. The strap is often worn so that it diagonally crosses the body, with the bag hanging on the opposite hip, rather than hanging directly down from the shoulder. The back of a satchel extends to form a flap that folds over to cover the top and fastens in the front. Unlike a briefcase, a satchel is soft-sided."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Satchel_and_laptop.jpg/330px-Satchel_and_laptop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Satchel"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Perfume_shelf_536pix.jpg/500px-Perfume_shelf_536pix.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Perfume_shelf_536pix.jpg/500px-Perfume